<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Landnámabók</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Book of Settlements</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Landnámabók, the Book of Settlements, is a medieval Icelandic work describing the settlement of Iceland from about 870. It names hundreds of the first settlers, their origins, descendants and the land they claimed, region by region around the island. Its earliest version is attributed to Ari Thorgilsson in the 12th century, and it survives in later 13th and 14th-century versions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/landnamabok.jpg" alt="Landnámabók" width="187" height="264" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LandnamabokManuscriptPage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
